{
  "format": "lithium-midi-map",
  "version": 1,
  "id": "millenium-mps1000",
  "name": "Millenium MPS-1000 / 600 / 850",
  "description": "The factory notes of Millenium's MPS-1000 and MPS-600 modules (their manuals' MIDI note lists, which agree), including the half-open hat (23), the hi-hat edge hits (26, 24, 22) and the pedal splash (21). The MPS-850's manual only says each pad's note can be set, so its notes here are inferred from the other two, not documented: check with the MIDI monitor. The MPS-450 and MPS-150 appear to share the layout too. The hi-hat follows the pedal where the module sends CC4.",
